From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chris Paslawski <chris@paslawski.me>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 14:32:02 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: msm8916-wcd: configure stock ThinkSmart DMIC clocks

The vendor ThinkSmart View device tree requests a 2.4 MHz DMIC clock.
Add the matching board clock limit and binding, select the fastest MCLK
divider that respects it, and program both the shared generator and each
powered decimator consistently. Decimator clock selection follows the
decimator rather than a DMIC widget's line number, so either input mux
routing works. Preserve MCLK/3 on boards without the new property.

Combine the reference port's four DMIC patches, including its credit to
justhalfbit for finding the per-decimator clock-selection issue. Retain
our existing Android channel routing, mixer gain and speaker driver.

Local adjustments reject malformed/out-of-range limits and unavailable
MCLK or an unachievable ceiling instead of silently exceeding it. Use a
wide multiplication when comparing rates, and propagate clock-register
write failures from the DAPM events.

Origin: Jetha Chan's ThinkSmart View DMIC series, with local validation
Source: https://github.com/jethac/lenovo-thinksmart-view/tree/1f99f7f09c26074d53064d7bb1fada262cbef10a/kernel/patches
Reference-revisions: 980e96b10c06534901bb403906c1228ac016718c
                    8bcced4a2833e6484dbccfe5c5d179a23c269291
                    aabb1c7b94f23ec8fda017f3e2d12b57c5705dd6
                    30b69dc186219443daaf0c75097c2735248a81dc
Base-commit: 755ffc44d5d8442adeec8bbaa02108478089c4d7
Apply in filename order within this project.

---
diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,msm8916-wcd-digital-codec.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,msm8916-wcd-digital-codec.yaml
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,msm8916-wcd-digital-codec.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/sound/qcom,msm8916-wcd-digital-codec.yaml
@@ -36,6 +36,15 @@
   '#sound-dai-cells':
     const: 1
 
+  qcom,dmic-sample-rate:
+    description:
+      Highest DMIC clock rate in Hz the microphones can take. The codec
+      uses the fastest MCLK divider (2, 3, 4, 6 or 16) whose output does
+      not exceed it. If absent, the DMIC clock remains MCLK / 3.
+    $ref: /schemas/types.yaml#/definitions/uint32
+    minimum: 600000
+    maximum: 6144000
+
 required:
   - compatible
   - reg
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/apq8053-lenovo-cd-18781y.dts
@@ -423,6 +423,10 @@
 
 &lpass {
 	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&lpass_codec {
+	qcom,dmic-sample-rate = <2400000>;
 };
 
 &wcd_codec {
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/msm8916-wcd-digital.c b/sound/soc/codecs/msm8916-wcd-digital.c
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/msm8916-wcd-digital.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/msm8916-wcd-digital.c
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 // SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0
